# Keeps the build context small and stops local state from leaking into a layer.
# Read by buildah/podman; `docker build` only looks for .dockerignore, so a Docker
# user needs to symlink one (see docs/container.md) - there is deliberately no
# second checked-in copy to drift out of sync.

.git
.github
# ...except the workflow files: .devcontainer/Dockerfile reads the pinned tool versions out
# of them at build time (via `just install-pinned`). The Containerfile build never copies
# them, so this only widens what that build *could* see, by about 40 KB.
!.github/workflows
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
coverage

# Locally-generated scan output (see .gitignore)
*.sarif
sbom.cdx.json
gitleaks
gitleaks_*.tar.gz
gitleaks_*_checksums.txt

*.log
*.local
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode

Containerfile*
.containerignore
docs
*.md
